    "round": "sounds-r3",
    "note": "The rhythmic half of the harmonic layer, one event name for five keyboard patches that `p.preset` chooses between — the electric piano, the rhodes, the glass, the organ and the pluck — each a row of its own; a note that names none, or one the table has not, plays the rhodes.",
    "notes": {
      "timbres": "Timbre to row, each struck as it is.",
      "knobs": "The keyboard's ranges (PLAN-MODULATION M1): five patches behind one name, so each default is the median of the five — 1900/2600/1800/2500/2000 Hz of corner, 0.30/0.32/0.37/0.72/0.048 of sustain, 30/22/24/9/11 ms of attack — and what a knob moves is a factor on whichever patch is playing; a setting in absolute hertz would make one instrument out of five. The ceiling on brightness is the one the voice has always had: the note's own lowpass is clamped at 9 kHz. The grain (round SPARK-1) is a factor on the edge and the strike a place writes, one at the house; its measured slope is the keys alone under the house's edge against none, seed 1 theme two, +0.002 LU."
    }
